    "note": "Read Amended 2018-06-14 (text of both later floor votes; the first vote on 2018-05-25 was on an earlier amended text not read). The bill strikes 'handgun' / 'pistol, revolver, or other firearm capable of being concealed upon the person' and inserts 'firearm' in sections 26835, 27535, 27540 and 27590. Section 26835 version amended is the one added by Ch. 825, Stats. 2017, operative Jan 1, 2019. The saved text also includes struck, unrelated Education Code spot-bill text from an earlier version."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 27535 (Penal Code): (a) A person shall not make an application to purchase more than one firearm within any 30-day period.\nSection 27535 (Penal Code): (14) The purchase of a firearm, other than a handgun, by a person who possesses a valid, unexpired hunting license issued by the Department of Fish and Wildlife. (15) The acquisition of a firearm, other than a handgun, at an auction or similar event conducted by a nonprofit public benefit or mutual benefit corporation to fund the activities of that corporation or local chapters of that corporation.\nSection 27535 (Penal Code): (c) For the purposes of paragraphs (14) and (15) of subdivision (b), the frame or receiver of a firearm is a handgun unless the frame or receiver listed in the application to purchase and delivered to the recipient is equipped with, is attached to, or is concurrently accompanied by, a barrel of 16 inches or greater in length.\nSection 27540 (Penal Code): (f) A firearm shall not be delivered whenever the dealer is notified by the Department of Justice that within the preceding 30-day period the purchaser has made another application to purchase a firearm and that the previous application to purchase did not involve any of the entities or circumstances specified in subdivision (b) of Section 27535.\nSection 27590 (Penal Code): (e) (4) For purposes of this subdivision, each application to purchase a firearm in violation of Section 27535 is a separate offense.\nSection 26835 (Penal Code): (h) “NO PERSON SHALL MAKE AN APPLICATION TO PURCHASE MORE THAN ONE FIREARM WITHIN ANY 30-DAY PERIOD AND NO DELIVERY SHALL BE MADE TO ANY PERSON WHO HAS MADE AN APPLICATION TO PURCHASE MORE THAN ONE FIREARM WITHIN ANY 30-DAY PERIOD.”"
}